WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.247
(Theme from Seinfeld)

00:00:01.247 --> 00:00:03.089
- [Jonathan] When Seinfeld first started

00:00:03.089 --> 00:00:06.248
none of us expected it to last.

00:00:06.248 --> 00:00:10.370
I was in charge of the music,
I turned that mother out.

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:12.262
(finger snapping and
mouth popping with rhythm)

00:00:12.262 --> 00:00:15.262
(audience laughter)

00:00:17.377 --> 00:00:18.781
- [Narrator] Jonathan Wolff is the

00:00:18.781 --> 00:00:20.806
man behind Seinfeld's iconic sound.

00:00:20.806 --> 00:00:22.292
(Theme from Seinfeld)

00:00:22.292 --> 00:00:25.222
But what even the most
dedicated fans may not realize,

00:00:25.222 --> 00:00:26.970
is that the theme song was actually

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:28.726
different for every episode.

00:00:28.726 --> 00:00:33.154
- I have no idea how many
themes we did for Seinfeld.

00:00:33.154 --> 00:00:37.894
I knew that each monologue
was gonna be different,

00:00:37.894 --> 00:00:39.309
'cause he tells different jokes.

00:00:39.309 --> 00:00:42.345
The timing, the length,
had to be adjustable

00:00:42.345 --> 00:00:44.441
in a way it would still hold water

00:00:44.441 --> 00:00:47.046
and still sound like the Seinfeld theme.

00:00:47.046 --> 00:00:50.450
Each monologue had its own recording

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:53.270
of the Seinfeld theme
to match those timings.

00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:57.270
- Old people in Florida, they
drive slow and they sit low.

00:00:57.270 --> 00:00:58.920
(Theme from Seinfeld)

00:00:58.920 --> 00:00:59.818
Right?

00:00:59.818 --> 00:01:02.088
- [Narrator] It all started
with a phone call from Jerry.

00:01:02.088 --> 00:01:02.921
- Hello?

00:01:02.921 --> 00:01:03.820
- [Man On Phone] Jerry?

00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:06.126
- [Narrator] When Jonathan first
began to compose the theme,

00:01:06.126 --> 00:01:08.223
he knew he wanted to use unique sounds

00:01:08.223 --> 00:01:10.529
that didn't drown out Jerry's voice.

00:01:10.529 --> 00:01:13.488
He ended up using his own
fingers and mouth as instruments.

00:01:13.488 --> 00:01:17.183
(finger snapping and
mouth popping with rhythm)

00:01:17.183 --> 00:01:19.062
- And I had his attention.

00:01:19.062 --> 00:01:20.528
- [Jerry] It's like the
Declaration of Independence,

00:01:20.528 --> 00:01:22.292
who's gonna read that?

00:01:22.292 --> 00:01:23.930
- [Narrator] After that Jonathan

00:01:23.930 --> 00:01:26.332
spent time watching Jerry on T.V.

00:01:26.332 --> 00:01:27.871
He noticed something.

00:01:27.871 --> 00:01:30.714
- I watched his HBO special,

00:01:30.714 --> 00:01:34.881
and noticed that Jerry has a
lyrical delivery to his jokes.

00:01:36.644 --> 00:01:39.561
And I put a clock on it, about 110.

00:01:41.473 --> 00:01:45.541
And that became the tempo
of the Seinfeld theme.

00:01:45.541 --> 00:01:47.763
The bass line for Seinfeld,

00:01:47.763 --> 00:01:50.263
(piano music)

00:01:51.344 --> 00:01:52.392
so simple.

00:01:52.392 --> 00:01:55.543
It can start and stop for his jokes,

00:01:55.543 --> 00:01:58.197
(piano music)

00:01:58.197 --> 00:01:59.426
hold for laughs,

00:01:59.426 --> 00:02:00.384
(audience laughter)

00:02:00.384 --> 00:02:03.331
and in that way I could
architect each piece

00:02:03.331 --> 00:02:06.063
of music for each monologue LEGO-style.

00:02:06.063 --> 00:02:08.563
(piano music)

00:02:11.971 --> 00:02:15.926
And that is how the
Seinfeld theme was born.

00:02:15.926 --> 00:02:18.380
- [Jerry] Oh my God, this drawer
is filled with Froot Loops.

00:02:18.380 --> 00:02:20.248
- [Narrator] In the end, Jonathan's music

00:02:20.248 --> 00:02:22.144
almost didn't make it onto the show.

00:02:22.144 --> 00:02:25.549
- Jerry loved the music,
Larry David loved the music.

00:02:25.549 --> 00:02:29.100
Everybody on board, except the network.

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:32.448
The notes were: what is this music?

00:02:32.448 --> 00:02:33.690
What is that instrument?

00:02:33.690 --> 00:02:35.996
Could we not afford real music?

00:02:35.996 --> 00:02:38.663
It's distracting, it's annoying.

00:02:39.755 --> 00:02:42.011
- [Narrator] But Larry
David wasn't having it.

00:02:42.011 --> 00:02:44.976
- Larry David, the hero of this story,

00:02:44.976 --> 00:02:47.823
liked that it was annoying.

00:02:47.823 --> 00:02:52.332
Said, "Don't you dare. Wolff
you're done here, get out."

00:02:52.332 --> 00:02:55.277
And I left and the music
stayed in the picture.

00:02:55.277 --> 00:02:58.444
(Theme from Seinfeld)

00:03:01.577 --> 00:03:04.994
(single signaling sound)

